From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:42:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/36] sched: overlap ubatches under -sm tensor -- async
 graph-input views, async CPU-split output, deferred input wait

The host waited on every split for a view of a graph input (96 waits, ~1 s per 4096-token prefill ubatch:
the GPU queue emptied before each split) and copied the CPU-split token embeddings synchronously at the head
of every ubatch (FINDINGS 881).

- GGML_SCHED_ASYNC_INPUT_VIEWS (default 1): a contiguous view of a pinned graph input takes the async upload
  with the recorded upload event, unless a non-view node writes its root (written_inputs, per split_graph).
- GGML_SCHED_ASYNC_CPU_OUT (default 1): a large pinned CPU-split output is uploaded asynchronously with the
  upload event; every host-backend split waits for pending uploads first and no prefetch runs while one is
  pending.
- ggml_backend_sched_defer_input_wait (one-shot) + LLAMA_DEFER_INPUT_WAIT (default 1): process_ubatch builds
  and allocates the next graph without waiting for the uploads and waits just before set_inputs. Other
  alloc_graph callers keep the wait. LLAMA_DEFER_INPUT_WAIT_CANARY=1 skips that wait (test only).
- GGML_META_STAGE_HOST_WAIT (default 1): the meta stage ring host-waits a slot's free event before reuse.
- GGML_MOE_ORDER_EV_RING (default 1): the MoE staging order event is a host-synced ring of 16 per device.

The view, CPU-output and deferred-wait paths run only on a scheduler with a META (-sm tensor) backend; a
plain device (1 GPU, -sm layer) keeps the old ordering. sched_free waits for pending uploads.

Same bytes, ordering only (FINDINGS 882).
